    m_Alignment: 1
    m_AlignByGeometry: 0
    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: "How do you reconstruct history? Most of the time it\u2019s educated assumptions,
    but other times historians can get lucky, like with this model for example.\nIn
    1920, during an excavation of a tomb of the Royal Chief Steward Meketre, a small
    hidden room filled with 24 next to perfectly preserved models of life in ancient
    egypt were found. \n\nThis scene in particular is based off this model of a slaughterhouse
    which is dated to approximated 1980 BCE, to the middle Kingdom of Egypt.\n"
