    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: 'Like most ancient civilizations, the Egyptians were intensely religious.
    They told vivid myths and stories that explained the natural world.


    The
    Egyptians believed that every day the sun god Ra would carry the sun across the
    heavens. When it became night, he take the sun and would travel across the lakes
    beyond the sky, accompanied by other gods and beset by all the evils of the Underworld.
    He would still return every morning to make the journey across the sky.

'
