    m_Alignment: 1
    m_AlignByGeometry: 0
    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: "The Egyptians invented techniques for weaving linens together. The upper
    class wore more transparent linens, while the lower class wore thicker fabrics.
    Generally these types of clothing were made from flax plant. \n\n\nSimilar to
    the slaughterhouse scene, the Egyptians recorded the lives of weavers into hieroglyphs
    and models, so the workers could follow the buried into the afterlife. There
    are many wooden models of day to day life in Egypt due to to this belief. \n\n\n"
