    m_FontStyle: 0
    m_BestFit: 1
    m_MinSize: 0
    m_MaxSize: 50
    m_Alignment: 1
    m_AlignByGeometry: 0
    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: "For a thousand years Egypt was a collection of small kingdoms, but around
    3,000 BC, a civil war began. When the dust cleared and the blood washed from
    the Nile, a Pharaoh led Egypt. Historians mostly agree that this pharaoh was
    either called Narmer or Menes. \n\n\nThe Pharaohs would lead Egypt for the next
    4000 years, transforming the collection of kingdoms into a single unified empire
    whose cultural influence extends even to today. \n"
