    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: "The Nile River was the lifeblood of Egyptian society. Every year, the
    river would flood, leaving behind fertile soil where the Egyptians could plant
    crops like barley, wheat and flax. \n\nThe river was also flush with life: hippopotamus
    and crocodiles swam freely, and the abundance of fish helped feed the growing
    Egyptian society. \n\n\n"
