    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: "The first cities of Egypt were small and dirty by modern standards, mud
    houses packed together haphazardly. What helped hold these communities together
    were shared beliefs in the gods. \n\nOver the 7,000 years of the Egyptian Empire,
    over 2,000 gods were worshipped, each god having their own set of temples and
    cult followings. \n\n\n"
